      "dc:description": "Transport of mineral, and overburden masses presents main problem in surface mining. In Rhenish lignite mining railroad trains hauling up to 1650 tons of overburden have necessitated development of heavy duty track, as well as rolling stock. In view of substantial depth of pits rubber belt conveyors capable of carrying up to 17.000 tph have proven to be most economical. Trends of further development are discussed.",
