      "dc:description": "Surface mining of lignite seam requires lowering of water table which may have damaging effect on adjacent wells and agriculture as well as cause subsidence of surface (between 0 and 5 ft as observed in East German lignite mining); in Germany as in most European countries mining industry is liable for damages to surface installations-building, roads, water pipe lines, electric cables, etc; it appears therefore necessary to predetermine magnitude (horizontal and vertical) of subsidence and paper presents techniques therefore.",
